---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { layers, layerUrl } from '../data/maps';
---
<Layout title="Data & sources">
  <main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><h1>A clear view of the data.</h1><p>Know what you’re looking at, and where it comes from.</p></div>
  <p class="sample-notice"><strong>Two types of data.</strong> Voting layers come from the uploaded GeoJSON files. Community layers and events are demonstration content.</p>
  <div class="prose"><h2>Map layers</h2><p>Each layer is a GeoJSON FeatureCollection in WGS84 coordinates (longitude, latitude). The uploaded voting layers retain their supplied geometry and attributes. Community layers are illustrative and include a <code>sample: true</code> property; events are fictional.</p>
    <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Dataset</th><th scope="col">Content</th><th scope="col">GeoJSON</th></tr></thead><tbody>{layers.map(layer => <tr><th scope="row">{layer.name}</th><td>{layer.description}</td><td><a href={layerUrl(layer.id)} download aria-label={`Download ${layer.name} GeoJSON`}><Icon name="download" size={16}/><span class="download-label"> Download</span></a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    <h2>Uploaded voting data</h2><p>The 34 polling-place records and 31 voting precincts come from <code>public/data/polling_places.geojson</code> and <code>public/data/voting_precincts.geojson</code>. They are served directly without changing their attributes or geometry.</p><p>The polling file contains 17 records marked Active, 11 marked Historical and 6 without an activity value. All records are available on the map, with activity shown in their details. Precincts and polling records link through the supplied polling ID. This site does not independently verify whether a location is currently in use.</p>
    <h2>Street basemap</h2><p>Street tiles are provided by <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>, under the Open Database License. The basemap requires an internet connection. You can turn it off and continue to explore the sample layers.</p>
    <h2>Community events</h2><p>The listings are authored demonstration content, not a live event feed. Calendar files label every entry “[SAMPLE]” and include the fictional-event notice. Dates use the America/New_York time zone.</p><a class="text-link" href="/events.ics" download>Download the sample calendar <Icon name="download" size={18}/></a>
    <h2>Replacing sample content</h2><p>Maintainers can replace the files in <code>public/data/</code> and update the map definitions in <code>src/data/maps.ts</code>. Event records live in <code>src/data/events.json</code>. Publish verified source information and review the notices when switching to production content. The project README explains the update and deployment workflow.</p>
  </div></main>
</Layout>
<style>@media(max-width:450px){.download-label{display:none}.prose td,.prose th{padding:12px 5px;font-size:12px}}</style>
